# Build/testing
- Discover and follow documented build commands; preserve VS/CMake conventions.
- Add pure-logic tests where game behavior cannot be unit tested.
- Compilation alone does not verify game-state behavior.
- Review callback registration/teardown explicitly.
- Persistence parsers need malformed/old-version tests.
- Prefer cheap falsification and preflight before heavyweight validation; see `.cursor/rules/heavy-validation-economy.mdc` and `docs/ai/AI_SOFTWARE_FACTORY.md`.
- Do not declare completion while relevant build/tests fail.
- State exactly which checks ran and distinguish unrun checks (**NOT RUN due to known blocker**) from passed checks; do not claim PASS when mandatory evidence is missing (**acceptance BLOCKED**).
